{"id": "EUVD-2026-101138", "enisaUuid": "c861eb29-f4b9-35bd-8f4c-a7f2c4c1909c", "description": "MuJS 1.3.6 before 1.3.9 contains a heap out-of-bounds read and write vulnerability in Array.prototype.sort that allows attackers to corrupt memory by inflating a simple array's length. Attackers can supply JavaScript that enlarges a dense array's length and calls sort, causing Ap_sort_cmp and Ap_sort_swap to access slots past the buffer and crash the process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:13:59", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/mujs-array-length-flat-oob", "https://codeberg.org/ccxvii/mujs/src/commit/307f18c4216420f2f56e22d8e7040baa39a6304a/jsarray.c#L245", "https://codeberg.org/ccxvii/mujs/commit/32064e10caa45e68fc87331ca53d042049cc9396", "https://mujs.com/downloads/", "https://codeberg.org/ccxvii/mujs", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/mujs-1.3.6-before-1.3.9-heap-out-of-bounds-read-write-via-array-prototype-sort"], "aliases": ["GHSA-45w2-9pc7-5crm", "CVE-2026-110715"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5969cd9e-f7c6-367c-8000-e71135188518", "product": {"name": "MuJS", "vendor": {"name": "MuJS"}}, "product_version": "1.3.6 <1.3.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0b599507-5bbb-33aa-8e3a-42557895426b", "vendor": {"name": "Artifex Software"}}], "isExploited": false}